WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.999
Meera Reed: Years ago, in the height of summer,
my father told my brother and me a story.

00:00:05.999 --> 00:00:10.100
He only told it once, and he refused to speak
of it ever again.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:15.320
When he was a young man in the Year of the
False Spring, a great southern lord held the

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.939
largest tourney Westeroshad ever seen in the
largest castle Westeros had ever seen.

00:00:20.939 --> 00:00:25.509
Knights and lords from across the Seven Kingdoms
made their way, drawn by the spectacle and

00:00:25.509 --> 00:00:27.279
the size of the champion's purse.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:32.610
Even the king was rumored to be attending,
though none had seen him in years.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:37.000
Ours is a small house, and my father had come
only to be part of the magnificence, whose

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.380
like he'd never see again.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:43.130
One afternoon, he was walking across the field
enjoying the warm spring day, when he was

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.050
set upon by three squires.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.800
None were older than fifteen, yet all were
bigger than him.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.400
This was their world, as they saw it, and
he had no right to be there.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.380
They snatched away his spear and knocked him
to the ground, cursing him for a frog-eater.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:00.170
Every time he tried to rise they shoved him
down and kicked him when he curled up on the

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.170
ground.

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:03.840
But then they heard a shout.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.640
"That's my father's man you're kicking!" howled
the she-wolf.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:12.100
Lyanna Stark, the young daughter of Lord Rickard
Stark, Warden of the North, and my father's

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.100
liege lord.

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.729
Lyanna laid into the squires with a tourney
sword, scattering them all.

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:20.810
My father was bruised and bloodied, so she
took him back to her tent to clean his cuts

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:22.710
and bind them up with linen.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:28.229
There he met her brothers — Wild Brandon
who led them, quiet Eddard and Benjen, who

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:30.140
was the youngest of the four.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:35.030
That evening, there was to be a feast in Harrenhal
to mark the opening of the tourney, and Lyanna

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:39.090
insisted that my father attend, as he was
of high birth with as much a right to a place

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.810
on the bench as any other man.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.900
She was not easy to refuse, this wolf maid,
so my father borrowed suitable clothes from

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.940
Benjen and went up to the great castle.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:51.980
Under Harren's great roof, my father ate and
drank with his fellow Northmen.

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:56.500
A black brother beseeched the knights to join
the Night's Watch, to snickers and smiles.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:01.290
Prince Rhaegar sang a song so sad that it
brought tears to Lyanna's eyes, but when Benjen

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:03.490
teased her for it, she poured wine over his
head.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.580
Lord Baratheon drank down a knight of skulls
and kisses in a wine-cup war.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:12.620
My father remembered a beautiful woman with
purple eyes who danced with Ser Barristan

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.959
Selmy and several others.

00:02:14.959 --> 00:02:19.010
As the end of the evening approached, Brandon
Stark asked her for one more dance on his

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:24.860
shy brother's behalf, and so Eddard Stark
shared the last dance of the celebration with

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.660
Lady Ashara Dayne.

00:02:26.660 --> 00:02:29.290
Abruptly, the hall went quiet.

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:33.880
The Mad King had come after all and was now
entering the hall with his Kingsguard.

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.959
He hadn't left the Red Keep in years, and
none could believe the state of him.

00:02:38.959 --> 00:02:45.060
His long yellow fingernails, tangled beard,
and ropes of unwashed, matted hair made his

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.240
madness plain to all.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:51.850
Nor was his behavior that of a sane man, for
in the blink of an eye, he could go from hysterical

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.780
laughter to weeping to rage.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:58.130
But when he commanded Ser Jaime Lannister
to kneel before him and swear the oath of

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:03.450
the Kingsguard before half the lords of the
realm, a cheer burst from the crowd, for Ser

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:08.580
Jaime was much admired for his courage, gallantry,
and skill with a sword.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:13.650
Amidst all this merriment, my father spied
the three squires who'd attacked them attending

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:14.700
their knights.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:17.599
Lyanna saw them too and pointed them out to
their brothers.

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:21.370
"I could find you a horse and some armor that
might fit," Benjen offered.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:24.170
My father thanked him but gave no answer.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:30.070
"Our people sit a boat more often than a horse,
and our hands are made for oars, not lances."

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:33.670
Much as he wished to have his vengeance, he
feared he would only make a fool of himself

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.780
and shame his people.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.819
Eddard had offered my father a place in his
tent that night, but before my father slept,

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:44.760
he knelt on a lakeshore looking across the
water to the Isle of Faces and said a prayer

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.700
to the Old Gods.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:51.050
The next day in the tourney, the three knights
whose squires had beaten my father unseated

00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.310
their opponents and earned a place among the
champions.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:59.409
But late in the afternoon, as the shadows
grew long, a mystery knight appeared in the

00:03:59.409 --> 00:04:00.409
lists.

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:04.650
He was short and clad in ill-fitting armor,
cobbled together from different suits.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:10.980
On his shield was painted a heart tree of
the Old Gods, a white weirwood with a laughing

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.500
red face.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.650
The mystery knight dipped his lance before
the king and rode to the end of the lists,

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.370
where the five champions held their pavilions.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.740
You can guess the three he challenged.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:26.890
Whoever the mystery knight was, the Old Gods
gave strength to his arm.

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:29.680
All three knights fell before him.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.591
None were well-loved, so the common folk cheered
the Knight of the Laughing Tree, as the new

00:04:34.591 --> 00:04:36.260
champion was soon called.

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:41.180
When the fallen foes sought to ransom their
horses and armor, the Knight of the Laughing

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:46.050
Tree's voice boomed through his helm and told
them: "Teach your squires honor.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:49.500
That shall be ransom enough."

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:54.870
Once the defeated knights chastised their
squires sharply, their horses and armor were

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:58.400
returned, and so my father's prayer was answered.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.750
The king was furious.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:04.340
In his madness, he suspected a traitor in
his midst.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:09.320
Perhaps even the newly-made Ser Jaime Lannister,
whom he had already sent back to the Red Keep.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:14.190
That night, the king asked Lord Robert Baratheon
to take to the lists and unmask the mystery

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.780
knight, declaring him no friend of his.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:22.860
But the next morning, when the heralds blew
their trumpets, and the king took his seat,

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.530
the Knight of the Laughing Tree had vanished.

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:32.150
All they ever found was his painted shield,
hanging abandoned in a tree.

00:05:32.150 --> 00:05:34.430
My father's tale ended here.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:39.620
He never spoke more of Harrenhal, though he
must have seen Prince Rhaegar's victory.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:43.680
Some whisper that Prince Rhaegar himself had
arranged to the entire tourney in secret as

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:48.389
a way to gather the great lords and address
his father's apparent madness, perhaps even

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:50.390
remove him from the Iron Throne.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:55.650
But when I asked my father about this, he
only shrugged sadly.

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:58.990
What Rhaegar intended, none can say.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.150
But all know what he did.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.890
Barristan Selmy: "Barristan the Bold" they
call me to my face.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:09.610
I know what they say behind my back; Barristan
the Old.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:13.570
I find myself visited by the faces of the
kings I have served.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.930
The faces of those I swore to protect.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:20.320
The faces of those I failed.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:21.590
Young Prince Aerys.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:26.199
For twenty years, his reign was peaceful and
prosperous.

00:06:26.199 --> 00:06:30.520
Aerys was well-loved by his people and respected
by his lords.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:34.430
But as years went on, Aerys' temper soured.

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:39.580
He became obsessed with dragons and fire,
and the swords of the Kingsguard couldn't

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:44.460
defend him from the enemies he saw lurking
in every shadow.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.180
My king went mad.

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:52.490
But there was hope; his son and heir.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:57.630
Prince Rhaegar was everything a kingdom could
hope for in a ruler; he was strong but gentle,

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.710
wise and cautious, and a good friend.

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:06.870
No matter the wounds Aerys dug into the realm,
we had faith that his son would sew it back

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:11.289
together again when he ascended the throne.

00:07:11.289 --> 00:07:16.460
Then came Lord Whent's tourney at Harrenhal,
the largest ever in Westeros.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.710
I unhorsed every man against me until only
Prince Rhaegar remained.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:28.990
We each set our feet in our saddles and lowered
our lances and charged, and I fell.

00:07:28.990 --> 00:07:33.229
Muddy and bruised, I then watched Rhaegar
present Lyanna Stark with the victor's crown

00:07:33.229 --> 00:07:38.900
of roses, though she was betrothed to Robert
Baratheon and Rhaegar himself was married

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.650
to Elia Martell.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.050
We all know what happened after.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:47.289
If I had I been a bit quicker with my lance,
had I chosen a faster horse, perhaps I could

00:07:47.289 --> 00:07:54.970
have spared the kingdom from the destruction
that came after.

